// attached to chione or starts immediately when you load into noon island
Narrator: You find Chione again the next morning, mixed in with the flow of Viridi who are busily milling about.
Amelia: What's going on here? #portrait:AmeliaSilly
Chione: Oh, Amelia, Noelle! Good morning! #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Chione: Remember the storm that brought you to our island? It's caused a bit of damage to the creatures’ homes in the forest, so we're helping them clean up. #portrait:ChioneNormal
Chione: We would've done so earlier, but yesterday was busy enough as it is by making sure no one was missing or injured. #portrait:ChioneNormal
Narrator: The sight of the village bustling about is familiar — you understand more than anyone how important it is to look after the people, first.
Noelle: The things about my boat supplies, and getting an audience with your Elder… #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Noelle: Those can wait until you're done with more important work. #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Narrator: In fact…
Noelle: …Is it alright if we lend a hand? You did give us food and shelter, so it's the least we can do. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Amelia: <i>You're volunteering me for work?!</i> #portrait:AmeliaSilly
Noelle: <i>I'll do most of the heavy lifting!</i> #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Chione: Oh! If you're sure, we really could use the help. #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Chione: If you head east from here, you should be able to find Bri. She's one of the villagers in charge of cleanup efforts! #portrait:ChioneNormal
Noelle: Got it! Thanks, Chione! #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
